```mermaid
%% State Machine Diagram: Payment Intent Lifecycle
%% Based on Chapter 4 — Domain Analysis

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pending: create intent

    Pending --> RequiresAction: 3D Secure / SCA required
    Pending --> Processing: payment method attached
    Pending --> Canceled: cancel intent

    RequiresAction --> Processing: customer authenticates
    RequiresAction --> Canceled: authentication fails

    Processing --> Succeeded: charge succeeds
    Processing --> Failed: charge fails

    Succeeded --> Captured: capture funds
    Succeeded --> Canceled: cancel (before capture)

    Captured --> Refunded: refund payment
    Captured --> [*]: fulfillment complete

    Failed --> [*]: retry or abandon
    Canceled --> [*]: order canceled
    Refunded --> [*]: money returned
```

## Diagram Description

The Payment Intent state machine models Stripe's payment lifecycle. The backend maps Stripe webhook events (`payment_intent.succeeded`, `payment_intent.payment_failed`) to these states via the `StripeWebhook.cs` handler.

**Key design decision**: The system maintains its own `PaymentIntent` entity state in parallel with Stripe's state to support the Bogus gateway (which has no external state machine) and to enable offline operations.

**Evidence**: `Module/Payment/Domain/PaymentCaptures/PaymentCapture.Method.State.cs`, `Module/Payment/Features/Storefront/Payment/Webhooks/StripeWebhook.cs`
